Offline the throw was identified as `std::length_error`
(`ThrowInfo .rdata` -> `CTA` -> `.?AVlength_error@std@@`), raised in
`0x3B01A0` after the name lookup (`0x3B0995`) via `0x1D0C9F0`'s
`[B+0x70] != 0` branch calling `0x15F420` (`0x1D0CCF3`). The "real" event scope
is not a valid parse context: `[ctx+0x30]` leads to a non-zero B, and the name
builder takes the length-taking branch. This is the failure that motivated the
synthetic parse context (§52, 2.2 of the analysis).

### 2.3 container grow branch with a zero vptr (crash at 07:47:32)

The same process family, after the synthetic ctx change but before the parent
container was pre-sized. Game banner:

    crashes 07:47:32

`minidump.dmp` 63,461,304 bytes, `exception.txt` 1,614 bytes under
`C:\Users\13229\Documents\Paradox Interactive\Stellaris\crashes\stellaris_20261023_074732\`.
The dump's faulting context (module base 0x7ff7d78a0000):

    crash rva 0x22c55f
    rip 0x7ff7d7acc55f
      rax=0x0  rcx=0x7ffa6affb0a8  rdx=0x0  rbx=0x1
      rsi=0x1ddcc9d20  rdi=0x0  r8=0x0  r9=0x7ff7d9a27aee
      r13=0x7ffa6affada0  r14=0x7ffa6affb0a8

and the disassembly around the fault:

    0x22c4aa: movsxd rbx, dword ptr [rcx + 0x14]   ; size
    0x22c4b1: mov    eax, dword ptr [rcx + 0x10]   ; capacity
    0x22c4b7: cmp    ebx, eax
    0x22c4b9: jne    0x22c58b                       ; fast path
    ...
    0x22c552: mov    rax, qword ptr [r14]           ; container vptr
    0x22c55f: call   qword ptr [rax + 0x18]         ; <== CRASH (rax = 0)

The fake parent handed `0x3B01A0` a container whose `+0x00` vptr was zero and
whose size == capacity == 0, so `0x22C4A0` took the grow branch and called the
null vptr. Fix: the synthetic parent now pre-sizes the container (begin -> a
16-slot buffer, capacity 16, size 0), which keeps `0x22C4A0` on its fast path
`0x22C58B`. A native test pins size==0, capacity > size, capacity >= 2 and that
the first write at `begin + size*8` lands at `begin`.

### 2.4 the chain worked, the driver judged the wrong snapshot (pid 11648)

The remote file was overwritten by the next run before the full text was read
back; the captured tail is verbatim:

    [c4] C2ExecDisarm rc=0
    [c4] probe stats: armed=1 token=68637 calls=4 fired=1 ctx_skip=0 invalid=0 instantiate_rc=0 patch_size=16 installed=0 verified=0 vtable=1 chain=0 pred_installed=0 pred_calls=1 pred_patched=1
    [c4] c bridge stats: armed=0 token=0 budget_left=0 calls=1 skip=0 busy=0 js_calls=1 js_ok=1 js_err=0 mismatch=0 last_rc=1 last_token=68637 last_value=1504
    Traceback (most recent call last):
      File "C:\temp\c2_exec_probe.py", line 318, in <module>
        sys.exit(main())
                 ~~~~^^
      File "C:\temp\c2_exec_probe.py", line 314, in main
        return run_live_case(pid, dll_path)
      File "C:\temp\c2_exec_probe.py", line 291, in run_live_case
        assert cstats.get("token", 0) == effect_id, (
               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    AssertionError: c bridge token 0 != effect_id 68637
    EXIT=1

`js_ok=1`, `last_value=1504`, `pred_patched=1`, `fired=1`, `chain=0`: the chain
itself completed in pid 11648. The assertion failed only because the `finally`
block re-read the bridge stats after `_cleanup()`, and `C2ExecDisarm` zeroes the
bridge's `token` (`armed=0 token=0`). The fix (`72a855d`) judges the live
pre-disarm snapshot (`contract_errors`) and waits for `fired==1 && js_calls>=1`
(`poll_done`), because the probe flips `fired` before `instantiate()` returns.

